=== Layer-2 Kernel Defense Demonstration (Runs A, B, C) ===

--- RUN A: Stock Unprotected xv6 Baseline ---
Action: Malicious script executes 'rm /important.txt'
Outcome: File /important.txt unlinked and deleted. DAMAGE CONFIRMED.

--- RUN B: Clean Benign Control on Patched Kernel ---
Action: Clean process reads /report.txt, creates /output.txt, runs /echo
Kernel Log: <none>
Outcome: Operations succeed normally. No false positives.

--- RUN C: Adversarial Attack on Patched Kernel ---
Action: Mark /inbox_cmd.txt untrusted; cat /inbox_cmd.txt | sh
Guest Execution: sh reads tainted pipe and becomes tainted
Kernel Refusal 1: sh attempts exec /rm -> taint: exec refused for pid 5
Kernel Refusal 2: sh attempts write /important.txt -> taint: write refused for pid 5
Kernel Refusal 3: sh attempts unlink /important.txt -> taint: unlink refused for pid 5
Final State: /important.txt intact and undamaged. SECURITY INVARIANT PRESERVED.
